[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known as one parser bug with one fix queued. The reports
say otherwise. They hold three different problems, and the queued fix covers only the first.

<Callout>
Not one issue. A parser fix will not stop the other two.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} />

Each problem has its own ticket: [parser](https://github.com/IgroztrAlle/MegaDev/issues/1),
[form hint](https://github.com/IgroztrAlle/MegaDev/issues/2),
[one-day shift](https://github.com/IgroztrAlle/MegaDev/issues/3).

## The three problems

1. **parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Tenants who write the day first
   get flipped dates. This is the bug the merged ticket describes.
2. **hint.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People at day-first
   tenants type what it says, and the form reads it their way. It shows up only on the form
   channel. Intake often tags these `parser`, because the symptom looks the same.
3. **one-day shift.** The date is off by one day, not swapped (Tuesday shown as Monday; two
   clients in different cities got different days for one meeting). Time zones are the likely
   cause. That is a guess, not confirmed.

## Why they were merged

The dedupe rule matches on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
"Wrong day on the invite" is true of all three problems, so they landed in one ticket. The
merge is the cheap choice during an incident. This page is the later split it allows.

## Checking this page

The table is computed from the ticket export at render time. Reports the export lists twice
are counted once. If the numbers here and the desk's live view disagree, trust the live view
and fix the page.

